  "term": "antiparkinsonian drug",
  "definition": "An antiparkinsonian drug is a substance used or studied for its ability to counter changes linked with Parkinson’s disease. In the source, this refers to a compound that reduced dopaminergic neuron damage, lowered α-synuclein buildup, improved dopamine-related functioning, and extended survival in animal models.",
